-fi, Jarboe, Lida Husik (entre la cantante pop y la pintora sonora), Robin Holcomb, Lisa Germano (Geek The Girl, «un viaje dantesco a la psique de una chica»), Tori Amos, Juliana Hatfield, Kristin Hersh, Jewel, Natalie Merchant, Cat Power (Moon Pix), Edith Frost, Lauryn Hill, Shannon Wright. Las «grrrls» más airadas: Lois Maffeo, Ani DiFranco, PJ Harvey (Dry, Rid Of Me), Liz Phair (Exile In Guyville), DQE, Aimee Mann, Sheryl Crow, Alanis Morissette, Neko Case. Y los paisajes sonoros de Björk, la cantautora más influyente de la década, Kate St John, Natacha Atlas, Heather Duby, Solex y Beth Orton.","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk y cantautores","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#women-90s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":134189779518137,"artist":"Aimee Mann","artist_id":213013104511993,"title":"I'm With Stupid","year":1995,"ess":0,"yt":"sTm7aZE6u6w","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautoras de los noventa","scene_id":198167102636761,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#women-90s","chapters":["Sección 6.6"],"pages":[[1,254,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":153,"text":"…Orange Years (1985) towards the baroque psychedelic-pop of the double album Thing Of Beauty (1989), whose sound was both dense and spaced-out. Aimee Mann's Til' Tuesday devoted their career, and particularly the romantic concept Everything's Different Now (1988), to delicate and introverted elegies.…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":254,"text":"…of shrieks, yelps, roars, whispers and wails on But Me I Fell Down (1994). The rebellious stance of these performers influenced Til' Tuesday's Aimee Mann, who resurrected a changed woman on I'm With Stupid (1995). Two veterans climbed the charts in Los Angeles with a mainstream sound and a mood that…"}],"podcast":[],